WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.495 --> 00:00:18.118
Jason walked into the gym and bumped into a tall, young woman.

2
00:00:18.158 --> 00:00:24.483
"Ooph!" "Jason, I'd like you to meet Allison.

3
00:00:25.484 --> 00:00:28.126
She's from Penny's Dog Shelter," said Mr.

4
00:00:28.166 --> 00:00:30.568
Dunn. "Penny's Dog Shelter?"

5
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.121
Jason was excited.

6
00:00:32.141 --> 00:00:35.122
"My mom and I like to visit the dogs there.

7
00:00:36.143 --> 00:00:37.344
My favorite one is Lucy.

8
00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:40.906
But we can't adopt her.

9
00:00:41.906 --> 00:00:43.027
My dad is allergic."

10
00:00:44.648 --> 00:00:45.688
Allison smiled.

11
00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:48.370
"I'm sure Lucy enjoys your visits."

12
00:00:51.691 --> 00:00:52.612
"And guess what!"

13
00:00:52.912 --> 00:00:53.653
cried Izzie.

14
00:00:53.673 --> 00:00:57.094
"We're going to visit the shelter tomorrow!"

15
00:00:57.114 --> 00:00:59.636
"Yeah," added Ethan.

16
00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:03.041
"Allison is going to show us how to make dog treats.

17
00:01:04.101 --> 00:01:05.742
We can bring them to the dogs tomorrow."

18
00:01:05.762 --> 00:01:09.763
"We're making peanut butter treats," said Allison.

19
00:01:09.783 --> 00:01:12.944
"Because almost all dogs love peanut butter.

20
00:01:13.944 --> 00:01:15.504
These treats are really easy to make.

21
00:01:16.485 --> 00:01:17.825
They only have four ingredients!"

22
00:01:19.065 --> 00:01:22.986
"Peanut butter and Izzie began to guess.

23
00:01:23.006 --> 00:01:28.268
"And water, whole wheat flour, and oats," said Allison.

24
00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:32.669
"Can you preheat the oven to 175 degrees, Mr.

25
00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:35.431
Dunn?" "Yes," said Mr.

26
00:01:35.471 --> 00:01:42.013
Dunn. "First we mix the dry ingredients in a large bowl," said Allison.

27
00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:45.515
"We need two cups of flour and one cup of oats."

28
00:01:46.755 --> 00:01:49.036
Ethan and Bobby measured the dry ingredients.

29
00:01:55.199 --> 00:01:58.200
we have to spray the measuring cup with oil," Allison said.

30
00:01:59.192 --> 00:02:01.233
"So the peanut butter will come out more easily!"

31
00:02:02.414 --> 00:02:04.216
Mr. Dunn knew what to do next.

32
00:02:04.236 --> 00:02:09.399
"Nina, can you please get one and a quarter cups of hot water?"

33
00:02:15.343 --> 00:02:17.605
Jason dumped the peanut butter into a bowl.

34
00:02:19.326 --> 00:02:22.248
Then Nina added the hot water while Jason stirred.

35
00:02:28.564 --> 00:02:32.267
"Now let's add the peanut butter mix to the dry mix," said Allison.

36
00:02:32.287 --> 00:02:36.751
"Combine until it becomes a nice dough ball."

37
00:02:38.132 --> 00:02:39.933
Izzie started kneading the mixture.

38
00:02:41.074 --> 00:02:43.256
Next Allison held up a rolling pin.

39
00:02:43.276 --> 00:02:45.938
"Now we're ready for the fun part!

40
00:02:47.039 --> 00:02:49.881
Jason, please sprinkle some flour on the table."

41
00:02:50.962 --> 00:02:53.924
Jason did, and then Izzie dropped the dough ball on it.

42
00:02:58.432 --> 00:03:03.155
please roll out the dough until it's about six millimeters thick," Allison said.

43
00:03:07.158 --> 00:03:08.819
love using rolling pins!"

44
00:03:09.399 --> 00:03:11.181
Nina said, rolling happily.

45
00:03:12.542 --> 00:03:13.822
Bobby laughed.

46
00:03:15.063 --> 00:03:17.425
"You look like a pizza maker, Nina!"

47
00:03:17.785 --> 00:03:19.126
he said.

48
00:03:20.647 --> 00:03:23.549
Allison picked up a cookie cutter shaped like a dog bone.

49
00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:27.652
"Everyone, grab a cookie cutter and start cutting out bones!

50
00:03:28.716 --> 00:03:30.177
Press the cutter into the dough.

51
00:03:31.417 --> 00:03:33.158
Wiggle it around and then lift it up.

52
00:03:35.179 --> 00:03:37.940
Then place the bone-shaped dough on the cookie tray."

53
00:03:43.142 --> 00:03:45.863
Jason lined up his dog-bone treats on the tray.

54
00:03:46.964 --> 00:03:51.145
He hoped Lucy liked peanut butter and that no one adopted her before tomorrow!

55
00:03:52.226 --> 00:03:54.267
He couldn't wait to give her a special treat.

56
00:03:54.287 --> 00:03:59.033
"Bake the treats for forty minutes," Allison told the campers.

57
00:04:02.816 --> 00:04:04.277
have to go back to the shelter now.

58
00:04:05.318 --> 00:04:06.378
But I'll see you tomorrow.

59
00:04:07.599 --> 00:04:09.040
Don't forget to bring the treats!"

60
00:04:10.241 --> 00:04:11.562
"Bye, Allison!

61
00:04:12.182 --> 00:04:13.143
Thank you!"

62
00:04:14.164 --> 00:04:15.725
The campers waved good-bye.

63
00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:21.709
The next day the campers arrived at Penny's with dog bones.

64
00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:25.252
Jason looked down the row of cages.

65
00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.694
He spotted his favorite dog right away.

66
00:04:28.714 --> 00:04:31.676
"Lucy!" he cried.

67
00:04:31.696 --> 00:04:33.917
"Here's a peanut butter treat.

68
00:04:34.838 --> 00:04:37.280
Just for you!"
